# date: mer. 11 nov. 2026 21:31:13 CET
specs/body.md:3:Design version A5, architecture section 17.8 (2026-11-10), refreshed to the inside model v6.2 (architecture 17.11, 17.15, 17.19, 17.24 to 17.27; exterior merged32f, and merged32g on US 7 and US 8), and to design version 7 (architecture 17.29 and 17.30; exterior merged32h: round joystick opening 5.60 with the separate frame FRM1, gloss black finish; the recording light is removed in v7 and the body has no part of it). All dimensions in mm. Axes: X along the finger (+X fingertip), Y across (-Y is the joystick side, the side the thumb works; the older name "+Y thumb side" is retired, 17.11), Z up. Angles are measured around the finger from the top of the band; minus is the joystick side (the joystick is at -78 degrees on US 9 to 13, motor at -44 degrees on US 9; the values per ring size are in the last section).
specs/body.md:14:Titanium grade 5 (Ti-6Al-4V), machined from bar (architecture 17.29). Reason: strength at 0.4 to 0.6 mm walls, skin-safe, takes the gloss black coating. The joystick frame FRM1 is the same material and is coated in the same batch as the body (specs/joystick-nub.md).
specs/body.md:72:| joystick frame FRM1 | 5.40 mm outer diameter, 4.80 bore, 1.30 long | ISO 2768-f on both diameters | separate part (specs/joystick-nub.md), bonded in the opening with 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black, 0.10 mm radial gap; 0.80 under the band surface to 0.50 above it |
specs/body.md:109:3. Clearance between the motor and its pocket: the design partner answers. The joystick clearances are fixed in v7: frame to opening 0.10 radial, cap to frame bore 0.20 radial (specs/joystick-nub.md).
specs/body.md:115:9. Closed in v7: the joystick opening is round, 5.60 diameter, through the wall, with the separate frame FRM1 (5.40 outer diameter, 1.30 long, 0.80 under the band surface to 0.50 above) bonded in it (17.29; specs/joystick-nub.md). History: the opening 6.6 along the finger by 5.6 around the band with a rectangular frame (17.24) is removed in v7.
specs/cover-glass.md:3:Design version A5, architecture section 17.8 (2026-11-10), refreshed to the inside model v5 (architecture 17.23, 17.24) and to design version 7 (architecture 17.30, 2026-11-11: the recording light is removed in v7). All dimensions in mm.
specs/cover-glass.md:6:The formed cover glass over the whole top face of the block. The face is one arc across the finger, rolled into the side walls and at the two ends. The screen under it stays flat. The glass is bonded to the screen panel by 0.1 mm clear adhesive (ADH1) over the whole face, so no air gap shows the edge of the lit area (17.30). It is also sealed to the body's glass seat all round by a perimeter seal ring SEAL1, 0.05 thick (Z 2.70 to 2.75), in a seat lowered 0.05 inside the body (model v5; assembly.md step 23, conflict K-A4; architecture 17.23, 17.24; open item S26). The tape is not chosen and its compressed thickness is unknown. Black print everywhere outside the lit area, with no opening of any kind in the print. History: the 0.4 mm print window for the recording light (17.21) is removed in v7 (17.30); the ring's recording sign is drawn on the screen by the firmware.
specs/cover-glass.md:59:4. Seal: the seal tape and its compressed thickness (S26). (Before v7 this point also held the recording light window; removed in v7, 17.30.)
specs/cover-glass.md:65:design/architecture.md lines 417, 419 (17.1), 488 (17.8, wins over 17.7 line 478); 17.23 and 17.24 (seal); 17.30 (the recording light is removed in v7, print with no opening, ADH1 over the whole face); design/architecture.md line 315 (16.1, lit area 10.8 x 21.6); design/bom.csv line 54; design/mech/thin/placement.csv (cover_glass).
specs/joystick-nub.md:3:Design version 7 (2026-11-11): architecture 17.29 (round joystick, gloss black finish) and 17.30, on the exterior merged32h (`design/look/s1/merged32h-report.md`, all seven sizes `RESULT PASS`). Pocket, dam DAM1, stiffener and switch cross are unchanged from the inside model v6.3 (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md` sections "Model v6" to "Model v6.3"). The file keeps its old name joystick-nub.md; the rectangular nub of version 6 and earlier is removed in v7 and replaced by the round cap CAP1. All dimensions in mm. "Along the finger" is X; "around the band" is the direction of the band's curve.
specs/joystick-nub.md:90:- Maker files: design/mfg/parts/joystick-nub/ and design/mfg/parts/joystick-frame/ still hold the version 6 shape (rectangular, removed in v7). Do not make anything from them. The lead regenerates both from the inside model v7; until then this page and the merged32h exterior are the definition.
specs/joystick-nub.md:91:- Drawing: design/mfg/drawings/joystick-nub.svg and .pdf, also version 6 until the lead redraws them.
