specs/main-board.md:51:Drawing: design/mfg/drawings/main-board.svg and main-board.pdf. STEP and STL: design/mfg/parts/main-board/main-board.step and .stl (index.csv: bare PCB outline only, 27.2 x 12.6 x 0.28; the thickness in the STEP is 0.28, the architecture says 0.3: open point 8). That STEP file is from model v6.2 and still carries the light guide hole removed in v7; the lead regenerates it from the inside model v7, and until then this page wins: no hole. KiCad files: design/ecad (open: Gerber, drill and pick-and-place not made).
specs/main-board.md:63:10. Closed in v7: the board has no hole (17.30); the copper rule round the light guide hole, LED1, R41 and Q2 are removed in v7.
specs/record-cap.md:5:A recording starts and stops by a long press of 1.0 s on the joystick's centre switch SW2 (architecture 17.11; specs/joystick-nub.md).
assembly/assembly.md:3:Basis: first written on design commit a0cf952 (2026-11-11, 00:50 to 01:00); brought to the inside model v6 and architecture 17.22 to 17.26 on the working tree at commit 6ccb258 or later (2026-11-11, from 05:38), what changed then is in `design/mfg/assembly/v6-update-notes.md`; brought to design version 7 on 2026-11-11 (architecture 17.29 and 17.30: round joystick cap CAP1 in a bonded round frame FRM1, gloss black finish; the recording light and its parts are removed in v7), what changed is in `design/mfg/assembly/v7-update-notes.md`. Step numbers are unchanged since the first issue, so other files that cite a step stay right. Each citation below was re-read by `check_assembly.py`, which prints the cited line (check.log).
assembly/assembly.md:23:Where files show an older state. The last measured inside model is v6.3 (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:407`); the inside model v7 (no light parts, round joystick) is being built by the lead and is not yet measured. The exterior of v7 is merged32h (`design/look/s1/merged32h-report.md:70`). The maker files in `design/mfg/parts/` are still v6.2 (they still hold the light parts removed in v7 and the rectangular joystick removed in v7); the lead regenerates them. The specs in `design/mfg/specs/` are brought to v7 (`design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:1`). This file follows architecture 17.11 to 17.30 wherever an older file differs, and says so at each step.
