assembly/assembly.md:78:Not used: the record cap CAP2 and its opening (removed, `design/architecture.md:546`); the wall microphone slots (removed, `design/architecture.md:657`); the recording light with LED1, R41, Q2, the light guide LG1 and the light plug LP1, the print window and the board hole, all removed in v7 (`design/architecture.md:834`); the rectangular joystick nub and frame, removed in v7 (`design/architecture.md:826`).
assembly/assembly.md:91:- **Check:** the board maker's electrical test of every net, thickness, warp (`design/mfg/specs/main-board.md:45`); no hole through the board (`design/mfg/specs/main-board.md:34`; the light guide hole is removed in v7).
assembly/assembly.md:96:- **Join:** every board part of `design/bom.csv` to the under face of PCB1, with solder paste and one reflow. The parts: U1 (`main_chip`), U2 (`power_chip`, nPM1304, `design/architecture.md:566`), R71, R72, U3 (`storage`), U10, U4 (`screen_supply_chip`), U5 (`mic_1`) and U6 (`mic_2`), Knowles SPK0641HT4H-1 (`design/architecture.md:654`, `design/bom.csv:9`), J1 (`screen_connector`), ANT1 (`antenna`), L2, L3, L4, C3, C12, X1 (`crystal_32M`), X2 (`crystal_32k`), L1, FB1, R1, R2, C1, C2, C5, C4, C6, C7, C10, C14, C11, L10 (`screen_supply_coil`), C21, C26, C27, C24, C25, C23, C22, C28, C29, C31, C32, C35, C36, R31, R32, R57, R58, R60, C60, U11 (`motor_regulator`, TLV75530PDQNR, at X 0.0, Y 4.2), C83 (`motor_cap_in`, X 0.0, Y 5.45), C84 (`motor_cap_out`, X 1.2, Y 5.0) (`design/architecture.md:705`, `design/mech/thin/placement.csv:19` to `design/mech/thin/placement.csv:21`; the places are the model's proposal until the board layout confirms them, `design/architecture.md:760`), U9, R61 and R62 (now on U11's enable pin, `design/architecture.md:705`), R66, R63, R64, R65, C61, C72, C80, C81, C82, C71, C73, C74, C75, C78, C79, C76, C77, C85, C86, C87, C88 (`design/bom.csv:67` to `design/bom.csv:69`), L71 (`power_coil_1`), L72 (`power_coil_2`). The motor switch and the motor diode of earlier versions are not fitted: they left the design (`design/architecture.md:705`). LED1, R41 and Q2 are removed in v7 and are not fitted (`design/architecture.md:834`). The test pads TP1 to TP22 (TP1, TP2, TP3, TP4, TP5, TP6, TP7, TP8, TP9, TP10, TP11, TP12, TP13, TP14, TP15, TP16, TP17, TP18, TP19, TP20, TP21, TP22) and the ribbon lands J_BAND_A and J_BAND_B are copper on the same face and get no paste [PROPOSED: reason, a solder bump on a test pad or a hot-bar land spoils the spring-pin contact and the hot-bar joint of step 16]. C13 is not mounted (`design/bom.csv:18`).
assembly/assembly.md:112:- **Join:** nothing is joined. The under face of PCB1 is cleaned of flux residue round the test pads TP1 to TP22 and the ribbon lands J_BAND_A and J_BAND_B, then dried [PROPOSED: reason, the spring pins of step 5 and the hot-bar joints of step 16 need bare copper; the paste and flux of step 2 are not named by any file]. History: this step fitted the light guide LG1 until v6; the light guide is removed in v7 (`design/architecture.md:834`).
assembly/assembly.md:185:- **Join:** first the frame FRM1 (titanium grade 5, 5.40 outer diameter, 4.80 bore, 1.30 long, coated gloss black in the same batch as the body) is bonded into the round 5.60 opening from outside the band with 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black epoxy, 0.10 mm radial gap filled all round (`design/bom.csv:82`, `design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:23`). Cure: 24 h at 22 C with no heat, the room temperature cure of 3M's data sheet for DP420 Black (revision June 2024, page 3: 4,500 psi overlap shear on aluminium after 24 h at 22 C); no oven, because the membranes of step 11 and the gaskets of step 12 are already in the body. Then the round cap CAP1 (`joystick_cap`, Makrolon 2407 colour 901510, shank 4.40 and flange as one moulded part, `design/bom.csv:81`) goes in straight from the bore: the 6.90 x 6.40 flange rises through the 7.0 x 6.8 pocket (0.05 mm on each side along the finger, 0.2 mm round the band), the 4.40 shank passes up through the 4.80 bore of FRM1 with 0.20 mm radial clearance, and the flange stops under the pocket roof, 0.05 mm below it, held on all four sides by the roof round the 5.60 opening (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:249`, `design/architecture.md:826`).
assembly/assembly.md:187:- **Before:** steps 10 to 12 passed. FRM1 and the body were coated in the same batch (`design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:22`). The bonding faces are degreased with isopropyl alcohol [PROPOSED: reason, the coated faces carry handling oil]. The DP420 has cured 24 h at 22 C before CAP1 goes in, because the cap is centred by the frame's bore and the frame must not move. The harness is not yet in the channel: the cap must go in before the switch head, which lies under the flange on the bore side (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:255`).
assembly/assembly.md:257:- **Join:** nothing is joined. The body's glass seat and the screen's top face are cleaned with isopropyl alcohol and lint-free wipes, then blown with ionised air [PROPOSED: reason, the cast of step 21 runs next to the block, and a speck on the seat breaks the line of SEAL1 while a speck on the screen shows under ADH1]. History: this step placed the light plug LP1 until v6; the light plug is removed in v7 (`design/architecture.md:834`).
